00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:04.320
It's been a while since I had a press conference in Japan. Maybe I overdid it.

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:06.610
You went overboard, Sana-chan.

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:10.700
Saying that in front of an audience,
if something goes wrong, it'd be disastrous.

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:13.330
Hey, Sana-chan,
are you listening? Hello?

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:17.920
I...

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:24.840
I'm very happy because you did great!

00:05:25.550 --> 00:05:27.930
Riho-san, I can't breathe.

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:34.480
Riho-chan, Naozumi-kun is still a
little too immature for this.

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:37.190
This is a live broadcast
brought to you by Babbit.

00:05:37.190 --> 00:05:38.900
Still hugging like this?

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:40.190
Isn't it embarrassing?

00:05:40.690 --> 00:05:42.400
Aki, good morning.

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:46.320
Now what, saying hello won't
hurt you, will it?

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:55.410
After I returned home, I carefully
thought over what you said.

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:59.170
My mind was very confused.

00:05:59.170 --> 00:06:02.250
I think I said something to you
that I shouldn't have said.

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:06.510
Saying that you should be more responsible and not make Sengoku-sensei angry.

00:06:06.510 --> 00:06:08.470
I really have some problems.

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:10.390
You really
didn't do anything wrong.

00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:13.180
Why should you apologize?

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:17.980
So please, don't put those words I
said into your heart.

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:20.940
Akito, just follow your own heart.

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:22.650
On the other hand...{checar}

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:26.860
If you don't pass the elementary
exam, I'll never forgive you.

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:30.240
Sorry, sorry, Fuka-chan.

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:33.740
Akito-kun, what did you say to
Fuka-chan?

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:35.700
Even if Fuka-chan is your
girlfriend...

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:39.750
...if you hurt a girl,
I'll get angry.

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:45.590
I'll go ahead first.

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:50.640
What?!

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:51.970
Annoying.

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:53.350
Tsuyoshi-kun.

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:58.180
- Good morning.
- Good morning, Fuka.

00:06:58.180 --> 00:06:59.520
Good morning.

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:08.110
Telephone call
from Takaishi

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:08.150
Telephone, telephone, telephone...

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:13.200
I just told him that he should be
more responsible...

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:16.370
...and not make Sengoku-sensei
hate him...

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:19.120
...but then Akito got angry.

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:22.500
But if he really didn't do
anything and is being hated for that...

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:25.880
...it doesn't matter how
responsible he is.

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:28.050
Really? You're right.

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:33.300
Just tell Hayama to beat
the crap out of the teacher.

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:35.430
Isn't that a quicker solution?

00:07:35.430 --> 00:07:36.350
Dummy!

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:39.060
Won't doing that
just make things worse?

00:07:39.350 --> 00:07:42.520
Never mind.
I found the wrong person to talk to.

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:44.940
If you and Hayama don't get along...

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:47.270
...you're welcome to
come back to me.

00:07:47.270 --> 00:07:48.690
What are you saying?

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:51.700
You should say this
to your quiet girlfriend Suzi-chan.

00:07:52.110 --> 00:07:55.870
Hello, hey, are you listening?

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:57.620
Hello?

00:07:57.620 --> 00:07:59.500
Yeah, I'm listening.

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:01.870
Sorry, I've only been talking about myself,

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:05.040
